# The core dev utilities (README invariant 7): what EVERY machine gets — the Mac, WSL, a rented GPU
# box, a shared server. ONE installer everywhere: `brew bundle --file=Brewfile.core`.
# Linux uses /home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew; LAND_HOSTS declares ~/.linuxbrew on no-root hosts.
# Prefer bottles at the standard prefix; source builds (including herdr) are allowed.
# Experiment toolchains belong to each repo's mise.toml; no global mise [tools].
# Command-path checks normalize qualified formula names and deduplicate conditional providers.

brew "bat"          # better cat (alias: p)
brew "eza"          # better ls (l, ll, la)
brew "fd"           # better find (f)
brew "gh"           # GitHub CLI — login is per box; never leave its token on a rented one
brew "git-delta"    # better diff
brew "jq"
brew "just"         # task runner (j)
brew "mise"
brew "ripgrep"      # better grep (gr)
brew "rm-improved"  # rip — the ONLY sanctioned file remover (rm is disabled)
brew "sheldon"      # zsh plugins → zsh/aliases.zsh
brew "herdr"        # agent multiplexer; `herdr --remote <host>` needs it on the remote too
brew "topgrade"     # `mise run up` (m up)
brew "zoxide"       # better cd (,)
brew "rustup"       # Rust manager and cargo proxies; opt/rustup/bin is exposed, toolchains stay per repo
brew "sccache"      # cargo's compiler cache — RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache is set unconditionally in the profiles
brew "fnox"         # secrets: Keychain (mac), age files elsewhere — scripts/secrets-push.ts fills a box
# A nonstandard Linux prefix would build core Bun/WebKit from source. The vendor's official
# Homebrew tap installs a verified release instead; Homebrew Bundle also owns its bunx alias.
if OS.linux? && HOMEBREW_PREFIX.to_s != "/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew"
  tap "oven-sh/bun"
  brew "oven-sh/bun/bun", trusted: true,
       postinstall: 'test -e "${HOMEBREW_PREFIX}/bin/bunx" || ln -s bun "${HOMEBREW_PREFIX}/bin/bunx"'
else
  brew "bun"        # declared core JS runtime everywhere: hooks, SSH commands and repo bins
end
brew "uv"           # declared core Python runner everywhere; Python versions stay per repo
brew "atuin"        # shell history (Ctrl+R)
brew "lazygit"      # git TUI (lg)
brew "jj"           # Jujutsu (config: jj/)
brew "direnv"
brew "fzf"
brew "dust"         # better du (du2)
brew "procs"        # better ps
brew "gping"        # ping with a graph
brew "sd"           # sed replacement
brew "choose-rust"  # cut replacement, binary `choose`
brew "broot"        # tree/navigator
brew "bottom"       # btm — config in bottom/, linked on every machine (declared nowhere until 2026-10-05)
brew "btop"         # system monitor (tmux prefix+G popup)
brew "tldr"         # better man (h)
brew "shfmt"        # shell formatter — `mise run fmt:sh` / `fmt:check` / `lint:sh` (file discovery); core
                    # since 2026-10-06: every machine that edits dotfiles runs `mise run lint`
brew "shellcheck"   # bash static analysis — `mise run lint:sh`; core with shfmt (same reason)
brew "kondo"        # build-artifact reclaim (`mise run reclaim:builds|pick`); core since 2026-10-06: rented boxes
                    # are the ones that fill up, and `mise run reclaim` failed on Vast with "kondo: not found"
